IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc7-s183-base.l4 -- plumbing shared by the modules of ccc7 (Criminal Code (Canada), Part VI, Invasion of Privacy, ss 183 to 196.1).
-- No provision of its own: the helpers and the cast of Part VI are carried under the first label of the range, `s 183 ...`,
-- because the naming rule makes every top-level name begin with a section label and no other part defines a name that begins `s 183 `.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
--
-- THREE-VALUED ANSWERS. Every decision function of ccc7 answers a MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE (the text says no in its
-- own words), NOTHING (not covered). The helpers below combine answers the way Kleene's strong logic does: one JUST FALSE decides a
-- conjunction (FALSE-kind of the caller's own branch), otherwise one NOTHING makes it NOTHING. They carry no FALSE-kind quotation of their own:
-- the branch of the caller that turns a helper's JUST FALSE into its own answer carries the quotation.

§ `Plumbing: three-valued answers`

-- A fact the person states becomes a three-valued answer.   (plumbing: the caller's branch carries the FALSE-kind)
GIVEN fact IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183 as a three-valued answer` MEANS
    IF fact THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Every answer in the list holds: JUST FALSE if any is JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE if all are JUST TRUE, otherwise NOTHING.
GIVEN answers IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183 three-valued all of` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS JUST FALSE) answers
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF all (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS JUST TRUE) answers
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

-- Some answer in the list holds: JUST TRUE if any is JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE if all are JUST FALSE (and the list is not empty), otherwise NOTHING.
GIVEN answers IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183 three-valued any of` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS JUST TRUE) answers
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (NOT (null answers)) AND (all (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS JUST FALSE) answers)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE NOTHING

-- The opposite of an answer: JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE swap, NOTHING stays NOTHING (a caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE).
GIVEN answer IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183 three-valued not` MEANS
    IF answer EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF answer EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

§ `The cast of Part VI`

-- Actors the Part names that the core's `Party` lacks (the core has no "agent of the state", no "police officer" apart from
-- "peace officer", no Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness, no "person who was the object of the interception",
-- no "party intending to adduce"): one actor type for the regulative rules of ccc7. Recorded in NEEDS-CORE.md.
@ref Criminal Code ss 183, 184.1(4), 187, 189(5), 195, 196 (the persons the Part names)
DECLARE `s 183 party under Part VI` IS ONE OF
    `s 183 an agent of the state`
    `s 183 a police officer`
    `s 183 a judge`
    `s 183 the prosecutor`
    `s 183 the accused`
    `s 183 the party intending to adduce the intercepted communication`
    `s 183 the Attorney General of the province`
    `s 183 the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness`
    `s 183 the person who was the object of the interception`
    `s 183 the Attorney General of each province`
